Package: cashomon
Title: CASHomon Model Sets and Permutation Feature Importance
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("CASHomon", "Contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "maintainer@example.org")
Description: Implements the finite-domain TruVaRImp algorithm of Ewald et al.
    (2026) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2603.15321> for finding near-optimal model
    configurations across model classes. Fits and verifies candidate models
    using 'mlr3', computes permutation feature importance for each retained
    fitted model using 'xplainfi', and visualizes explanation variability.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, utils, grDevices
Suggests: ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0), mlr3 (>= 1.1.0), xplainfi (>= 1.2.0),
    R6, mlr3learners, ranger, rpart, testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    knitr, rmarkdown, roxygen2 (>= 7.3.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
VignetteBuilder: knitr
